#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184236 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183918 :question/id #uuid "0431c02c-9a72-5d5b-ad75-550f413b74f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-10025" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c84e8bf0c80a5c57252ff368d0f59499b0299d4e59f49fdf738e3869f0bcf4f.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y = \\tan(Bx) + D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B + D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT =  \\dfrac{\\pi}{5} - \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\right) = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y = A\\tan(Bx + C) + D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT = \\dfrac{\\pi}{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2\\pi}{5} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{B} \\quad\\Longrightarrow \\quad B = \\dfrac{\\pi}{\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. The graph shows that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D = 1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB + D =\\dfrac{5}{2} +1 = \\dfrac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny = \\tan\\left(\\frac{5x}{2} \\right) +1.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050085 :topic/math-academy-id 1254 :topic/title "Combining Graph Transformations: Two Operations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050764 :topic/math-academy-id 654 :topic/title "Graph Transformations of Tangent and Cotangent"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86772212-906f-5549-b0a8-da556aa99a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183566} {:answer/id #uuid "649c3f40-f63c-5873-b39a-b3141cdea0d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183567} {:answer/id #uuid "703a8949-5d98-5297-8715-deee3aef7e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183568} {:answer/id #uuid "70512bc7-97c8-5498-9f79-6bf61335104b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183569} {:answer/id #uuid "7d76318c-ff9b-541a-b4dd-2ecf529dd032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183570}] :answer-field/id #uuid "179fae05-4da2-53cd-9be1-6068cea66c85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b461b10-efaf-5737-8be0-2296935fd388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398921} {:answer/id #uuid "f713561b-1443-55ab-a6f8-528c853237ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398922} {:answer/id #uuid "35eebbf8-cb3d-55be-881a-6d4dee741c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398923} {:answer/id #uuid "1304d7b1-7fd6-5fdd-8ab5-88b53194f932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398924} {:answer/id #uuid "03399f19-3885-5f0b-a462-01f7b14158b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03399f19-3885-5f0b-a462-01f7b14158b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398925} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a53e49d-1068-5089-bc50-b1b5ed69d2d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398920}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf5f1258-fe1b-5b76-b089-dbb4191effcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-65448" :question/problem "![](images/10/10912ded2166eb7ae28ee81c2936f008bf14eb288ec95969b822dd138be509d8.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\pi -(-\\pi )=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n2\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{2\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd899d43-38c7-5c0a-99fa-a8decf332a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183578} {:answer/id #uuid "233c624f-bad4-5f85-875a-d129007997c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183579} {:answer/id #uuid "243297e5-397d-5aea-99ed-895632bb8cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183580} {:answer/id #uuid "70e32dff-9a2a-5df3-b2fb-da2663102ccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183581} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3d28a6-25c5-5044-b64b-aa8808056e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183582}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b25c5c-7902-5676-844a-cdd0716ed88d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183577}] :question/id #uuid "30498f02-9ef3-55ca-84cf-796d6fb3816d" :question/math-academy-id "q-65547" :question/problem "![](images/16/1657098115279754d25cd67dc0a3afdbdebe6660ad483249054ea11bdea41ccd.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y = \\tan (Bx) + D$, where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $D - B$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "136e9a50-a407-5dae-bb44-6830ed03634d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250721} {:answer/id #uuid "71247e13-a93b-5580-b517-d8ff9b498733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251477} {:answer/id #uuid "878a709f-3d04-5bfc-a930-c231fd8f4d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251695} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd379a2-c52a-5f4e-8e55-bf89541c660a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252209} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2a82e3-36c7-5494-9ee6-1f44ba1cd0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "136e9a50-a407-5dae-bb44-6830ed03634d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250721} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf25f51e-e56f-50b4-a8b7-6e2bb7244cba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253162}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f5a48a1-5998-564e-8067-a60e891e1877" :question/math-academy-id "q-117795" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f920d90aa215300e720ace10bfec9292440d20f32c9b907854b984014f77427.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+(-3)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)-3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226ed9c2-7689-523e-8b19-51cec8859457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269567} {:answer/id #uuid "9496f9be-78ac-5c1d-87d1-26319ba1a036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270570} {:answer/id #uuid "b1108937-3dcd-5a86-b465-a26d9dae5c1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270850} {:answer/id #uuid "b195a681-69dc-577a-9b60-69ec56c83520" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270859} {:answer/id #uuid "bf896826-6cab-51c8-9d11-14de92c9b58c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9496f9be-78ac-5c1d-87d1-26319ba1a036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270570} :answer-field/id #uuid "9091b3e7-e4fb-59b0-9562-180d1542a3af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271766}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8e5a761-571d-5609-89c6-2c78742817c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-141974" :question/problem "![](images/2b/2b8bbc9ae6b8bf8c441c8e2b534fb159f8180833e1891baa094f988d6a362117.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $D-B?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\frac{6\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ units up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $D-B=1-(\\frac{2}{3})=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})+1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35381417-ae96-547a-8f09-c661f2a6392b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272859} {:answer/id #uuid "47db2918-1d4f-5d72-9867-d0717a28dfd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273001} {:answer/id #uuid "6403670f-9d16-5021-ae53-4275547be540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273245} {:answer/id #uuid "74dc3b36-73c9-54de-8452-14e52f6d4c12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273385} {:answer/id #uuid "ed688b95-443d-59f5-be09-dc3f86780692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed688b95-443d-59f5-be09-dc3f86780692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274488} :answer-field/id #uuid "34f320ed-c938-5762-b511-cc788825f43f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274726}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c15605a0-fccc-5892-a3b5-02a0bd086a37" :question/math-academy-id "q-143638" :question/problem "![](images/11/112ee04f02087fbf9f477a4cc002a7b24f7881e1ac2e37a1566ccc43e948cf0a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }=2.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $2$ unit down. Hence, $D=-2.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=2+(-2)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34eca68d-7384-5ac4-aae3-9fd3ad9100c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398167} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf81549-b73c-5aa8-ae6f-2eb529e3d650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398168} {:answer/id #uuid "4b365ba9-edc9-5d4f-9d0c-a4e1280cad8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398169} {:answer/id #uuid "95065041-df6a-55e2-ba59-eb39e1ef3c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398170} {:answer/id #uuid "4041d9b8-a50e-5114-a489-9911977efeb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebf81549-b73c-5aa8-ae6f-2eb529e3d650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398168} :answer-field/id #uuid "b20222d5-4d8b-5ef3-b5e6-cdd257fd9b17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398166}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ecbe368-922d-5a9f-956d-5a27886e10df" :question/math-academy-id "q-117796" :question/problem "![](images/92/9278723975d70fec73e313d0e164908ddd339231cb74f75b07c2edce14680111.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}-(-\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. Hence, $D=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Stretch and Vertical Shift of a Transformed Tangent Curve"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192585 :question/id #uuid "c700cc22-203a-5ad3-913c-e5eb507e22e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13995" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n${a + 4b = 1; 2a + b =-5$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $a$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $a$, multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$,\nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $a$ will turn into $-2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n{(a + 4b = 1)\\cdot (-2); 2a + b =-5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a - 8b &= -2 \\\\\n2a + b &= -5 \\\\\n(-8b + b) &= (-2 - 5) \\\\\n- 7b &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $a$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049060 :topic/math-academy-id 742 :topic/title "Introduction to the Elimination Method"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e0b7d00-1654-52b7-9052-7a91aba67a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191238} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6b863b-f16e-552b-a6e4-05539ba27cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191239} {:answer/id #uuid "11e4d5ce-3fc3-53e8-8584-1042acdeff24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191240} {:answer/id #uuid "41f6c130-1233-542f-a28b-1ce8647c5922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191241}] :answer-field/id #uuid "379e8fcc-29be-5846-9a9e-189e462ab1f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15818fb1-87d0-562d-b98a-b5e28f06c22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191243} {:answer/id #uuid "191da071-188e-5707-938f-7f3a2b084c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191244}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3bd31a5e-f325-573b-965a-e81ee45bc294" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191242}] :question/id #uuid "1d7ff6e0-7f69-5f77-a026-49d6c5918b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-210858" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n${x - y = 1; - 7x + 5y = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a45b4e3-546f-58ce-bc86-f21f14be794d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191246} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce11990-8f77-5ca3-bb7c-924e6d9f7e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191247}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f741ca69-46ce-51d3-89ee-ebd3b9b5298e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2d6ae65-382f-5725-8d12-368b3161c220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191249} {:answer/id #uuid "e5dd37b2-c127-522c-8a0a-7efbd395282d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191250} {:answer/id #uuid "2d811e29-d735-5f20-b57d-488fa19f4d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191251} {:answer/id #uuid "43aa771d-f31e-507f-a36a-818c77be68a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191252}] :answer-field/id #uuid "da2c168a-6d3a-5018-b549-be3fcba5455b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191248}] :question/id #uuid "35ea5fbe-0a0e-53a6-8872-3cafe1bfb9c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-210859" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n${3s + 4t = 8; s + 5t = 10$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations."}] :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192586 :question/id #uuid "eb7f1f32-1a5c-526e-878b-8046c4feb8c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13997" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n${3x + 4y = 2; x - 2y = 4$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$,\nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n{(3x + 4y = 2; (x - 2y = 4)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + 4y &= 2 \\\\\n2x - 4y &= 8 \\\\\n(3x + 2x) &= (2 + 8) \\\\\n5x &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805f8ad6-7fae-5b23-9e8d-6ae094055dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191254} {:answer/id #uuid "90021633-7a04-57cc-a6b7-c9aa58120746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191255} {:answer/id #uuid "ba18e7d3-a103-5f29-b2f2-a9cc52a7d7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191256} {:answer/id #uuid "48b2983a-4a87-59af-9b24-bfd7e5742c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191257}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e9765b05-9f5e-5ceb-9f0e-0d6c072cc44b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae9cab50-265a-5afc-82c8-311974f94350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191259} {:answer/id #uuid "1027a566-2403-5d1f-9d08-ec90c8bdf68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191260}] :answer-field/id #uuid "db50d077-69c4-51f2-8ce5-49723eab52fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191258}] :question/id #uuid "e332bfe2-c273-5ee4-850d-82761fba6c6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210947" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n${9x + 10y = 3; - 2x - y = 3$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae17497b-ef62-524c-a92b-99019b9aa220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191262} {:answer/id #uuid "0a5be49c-3115-56c4-9688-33ccf8c7dc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191263} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc752b7-923d-5615-9510-b559ab5b697e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191264} {:answer/id #uuid "6134cb91-ef2a-50fc-9cd7-decca8b927ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191265}] :answer-field/id #uuid "23a19cb8-4689-536b-b1f4-cbdf75104d4a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b479d9f4-f5f7-5706-9684-f1894b624f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191267} {:answer/id #uuid "c23d6f1a-f741-5c2d-9521-2a45acd5a695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191268}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e8772a-1d19-54ba-8ef4-473321fb514a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191266}] :question/id #uuid "eaa71162-ff27-5db0-a3a2-f11a9f212b35" :question/math-academy-id "q-211000" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n${3w + 2z =-1; 7w + 10z = 3$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $z$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $z$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations."}] :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192587 :question/id #uuid "f20f46d9-b799-57a2-90bc-12e6593e8655" :question/math-academy-id "e-13999" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n${2x + 3y = 8; x - 2y =-3$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n{(2x + 3y = 8; (x - 2y =-3) \\cdot (-2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3y &= 8 \\\\\n- 2x + 4y &= 6 \\\\\n(3y + 4y) &= (8 + 6) \\\\\n7y &= 14 \\\\\ny &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 2$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 2y &= -3 \\\\\nx - 2(2) &= -3 \\\\\nx - 4 &= -3 \\\\\nx &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=1, \\,y=2$, which can be expressed as $(1,2)$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b07de6e3-d564-59dd-ab2b-f52b2f6a8dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191188} {:answer/id #uuid "f9dc4fdb-fc7f-57b9-bbcb-171440bb6b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} {:answer/id #uuid "04165ac7-0685-5e0f-84da-400e81b14bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191190} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb7d195-ce50-55d4-aa09-3ee5c62715d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191191} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc0bdd0-bb80-5744-9913-d84b487d2594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191192}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3d02a81e-fa71-57d8-a298-b58e206ffcea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191187}] :question/id #uuid "4c0138a9-c275-57a0-80c9-430f32b2f421" :question/math-academy-id "q-18787" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n${4x - 5y = 0; 2x - 3y = 2$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x$.*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "1baa2398-4954-5c79-9541-1319e47e02cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191226} {:answer-field/id #uuid "652cda5c-8a31-5ce3-bccf-786c2da038cc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191227}] :question/id #uuid "96c8f94a-3d88-537c-8d5d-fa47a28c510f" :question/math-academy-id "q-208816" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n${4x + 3y = 5; - x + 7y =-9$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}} $$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable"}]}
